          <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">RamNode is the right pick for developers who want hourly billing flexibility without the standard annual lock-in, and who care about payment-stack variety (crypto + Alipay are rare at this price tier for US-hosted VPS). The five-datacenter footprint covers the practical transatlantic and US-East-West cases without overspending on locations buyers won't use. For US East/West + NL coverage on hourly billing, RamNode is a focused pick. For the absolute cheapest VPS or unmetered bandwidth, <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd's annual-special floor at $10.98/yr across 8 DCs</a> still wins. For APAC-heavy workloads, <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">LightNode's 40+ locations from $7.70/mo</a> covers the regions RamNode doesn't yet reach.</p>
